<!--
  The Today widget, compact: from its 250 by 180dp minimum, on every launcher below Android 12, and
  whenever it is shorter than 300dp (324 from 1.1x text; 346 and 374 in Urdu, Arabic and Bengali) (WidgetRenderer.TODAY_SIZES). The six times, each with the glyph of
  where the sun is, the current one marked. Rows are weighted, so they spread over whatever height the
  launcher gives instead of stopping a third of the way down (the owner's 1.4.0 screenshot). No header
  here, for the reason the 1.4.0 version gave: at 180dp a header pushed Isha off at a larger font.

  Sunrise is dimmed and is never the highlighted row, as on the Times screen. The foot holds the
  location chip and, on a projected polar day, the approximate marker beside it.

  Rules for every widget layout (WidgetResourcesTest fails the build on each): no android:text, because
  the launcher would resolve it in the PHONE's language; only classes a RemoteViews may inflate (no plain
  View, so hairlines and progress bars are ImageViews with a drawable); every text view hidden from
  TalkBack, the root carries one spoken sentence; every colour a resource, resolved by the launcher at
  each draw so the widget follows the phone's dark mode
  under the app's Theme "System" (Light and Dark pin them: the _fixed layout). Glyphs are drawn white and tinted here, for the
  same reason (lesson 130).

  The countdown is set in the light weight, Apple Clock style, and its size is written from
  WidgetRenderer in dp rather than sp: it is already about three times the body text, and scaled by a
  large font setting it pushed the prayer name off a 110dp widget. Names and times stay in sp.

  tools:ignore on the root, all three deliberate: the empty weighted LinearLayouts are the gaps that
  spread the content (HANDOVER lesson 142), the nested weight is the wide layout's two columns, and a
  compound drawable cannot be tinted per theme from a layout the way an ImageView's glyph is.
-->
<LinearLayout
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/widget_root"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
